                <pb facs="0273" n="173" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.1211/253: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at Nuevo
                        Laredo</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Robertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-22T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1920—7
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Fernando Iglesias Calderón will shortly visit Washington on special mission. He
                    leaves Mexico City June 22.</p>
                <p>Department desires that courtesies due distinguished private citizens be extended
                    to Calderón and his party.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
